---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Medical Disclaimer - TDEE Check"
  description="TDEE Check medical disclaimer: calculator results are estimates for education only and are not medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment."
  path="/medical-disclaimer/"
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Medical Disclaimer', path: '/medical-disclaimer/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink-900">Medical disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-500">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Estimates only</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      Every calculator on TDEE Check produces estimates based on population formulas such as Mifflin-St Jeor and
      Katch-McArdle. Individual energy needs vary because of genetics, muscle mass, medications, thyroid function, sleep,
      and many other factors. A result can reasonably differ from your true energy expenditure by 10 to 15 percent or
      more. Use the numbers as a starting point and adjust using your own tracked results over several weeks.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Not medical advice</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      Content on this site is educational and general in nature. It is not medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment, and
      it does not create a clinician and patient relationship between you and TDEE Check or its reviewers, including
      Farah Akram, Dietitian. Always seek the advice of your physician or another qualified health provider with questions
      about a medical condition, and never ignore professional advice because of something you read here.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Who should not use these calculators without guidance</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6">
      <li>People under 18 years of age</li>
      <li>People who are pregnant or breastfeeding</li>
      <li>People with a current or past eating disorder</li>
      <li>People managing conditions such as diabetes, kidney disease, or thyroid disorders</li>
      <li>Anyone whose clinician has given them specific nutrition instructions</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      If any of these apply, work with your clinician or a registered dietitian before changing your calorie intake.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Safe intake floors</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      As a general safety guide, most adults should not eat below 1,200 kcal per day for women or 1,500 kcal per day for
      men without medical supervision. If a calculator result falls below those levels, choose a smaller deficit or a
      maintenance target and discuss your plan with a professional.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Emergencies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      If you think you may have a medical emergency, call your local emergency number or go to the nearest emergency
      department. Do not rely on this website in an emergency.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
